OL,3,GNEWSAHelping families affected by
OL,4,Acancer after son's death
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mum has been helping other families
OL,7,Faffected by cancer after her son died
OL,8,Ffrom a rare form of the disease.
OL,10,FCallum was 18 years old when he died
OL,11,Ffrom Ewing sarcoma in 2022 after being
OL,12,Fdiagnosed in 2018 and, since then, his
OL,13,Fmum has campaigned to make more people
OL,14,Faware that cancers can affect young
OL,15,Fpeople.
OL,17,FJoanne McNulty said: "We went down to
OL,18,Fthe hospital four times because he
OL,19,F[Callum] had a pain in his back and
OL,20,Fthey kept sending them away because he
OL,21,Fwas so active... that's what they put
OL,22,Fthe pain down to."
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
